            "review_title": "Review at Nulla",
            "review_text": "Ravin Zhong\n31 contributions\n0\nQuaint little gem\nSep 2019 • Business\nAs I paced the pavement on Le Lai street, I made a natural jaunt into an aromatherapy store. I was half right. The other half was a cafe with a bar counter for those with a laptop you will love it. Not many seats lined up. Upon closer examination, you could probably tell this isn't really made out to be a cafe per se. It carries an assortment of handmade soaps, lip balms, herbs, spices even on sale in small quantities. There's even a chia seed dispenser among other dispensers lined up the shelf. A very clever concept of marrying retail, drinks and get this straight- neatly tucked upstairs they have a Yoga Studio. Thus, ensuring a work life balance well reflected in the cheerful disposition of the pretty owner. There's Vietnamese coffee on the menu besides usual cafe fare. A couple of detox smoothies are on serve here. It's a nice quaint little place to swing by after a stressful day at work to grab a juice or take away some ginger powder, curcumin or chia seed. \n\nThe changing landscape of Le Lai street welcomes another interesting addition in Nulla, purify your life.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 16, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-13",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
